WEBVTT

00:01.750 --> 00:03.560
<i>It's raining hard.</i>

00:02.140 --> 00:12.990
<b>32ND ANNUAL NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL DRAMA FAIR REGIONAL PRELIMINARY</b>

00:04.260 --> 00:08.510
<i>But the forecast says 
it should let up soon,</i>

00:08.510 --> 00:11.480
<i>so the regional preliminary for the 
National High School Drama Fair</i>

00:11.480 --> 00:13.830
<i>will proceed as planned.</i>

00:14.750 --> 00:18.220
<i>We ran into the major hurdle of 
losing our heroine the day before,</i>

00:18.220 --> 00:21.250
<i>but Iroha agreed to step in and fill the gap,</i>

00:21.250 --> 00:22.910
<i>so we avoided that disaster.</i>

00:23.730 --> 00:27.330
<i>Now all we need to do is exactly 
what we've been practicing.</i>

00:27.330 --> 00:32.010
<b>MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER HAS IT IN FOR ME!</b>

00:32.550 --> 00:36.800
<b>#12 "MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER 
REALLY DOES HAVE IT IN FOR ME"</b>

00:34.260 --> 00:35.820
It's me. Can I come in?

00:35.820 --> 00:36.970
Sure!

00:41.560 --> 00:45.790
Senpai! What do you think of 
my makeup? Perfect, right?

00:45.790 --> 00:47.980
So cute, it makes you wanna 
grab me here and now?

00:48.710 --> 00:50.400
It looks fine to me, I guess.

00:50.400 --> 00:53.730
That is the worst thing 
you could say to the girl you love

00:53.730 --> 00:55.200
when she just nailed her makeup.

00:55.200 --> 00:57.210
This is the problem with virgins.

00:57.210 --> 01:00.700
What kind of bugged rating algorithm is that?

01:00.700 --> 01:02.530
Also, you're not "the girl I love."

01:02.530 --> 01:05.120
The part about you being 
a virgin is true, though, isn't it?

01:05.120 --> 01:07.950
You're not getting past me.

01:07.950 --> 01:11.620
Being all alone with me in this tiny 
green room is getting you so excited

01:11.620 --> 01:14.750
that your manhood's bursting 
at the seams, isn't it?

01:14.750 --> 01:17.850
Iroha, you're mistaken about one thing.

01:17.850 --> 01:19.850
Oh? And what's that?

01:20.140 --> 01:22.100
I'm not a virgin.

01:20.180 --> 01:22.560
<b>SCHRÖDINGER</b>

01:20.550 --> 01:22.560
<b>MEOOOW</b>

01:22.560 --> 01:23.560
<b>WAIT, HE'S KIDDING, RIGHT?
WHAT? WHAT DOES HE MEAN?
HOW? HUH? WITH WHO?
FOR REAL? WHERE? WHAT?
WHY? WHEN? NO WAY!
WHAT? I DON'T BELIEVE IT!
NO, SERIOUSLY, HOW?
HE'S GOTTA BE BLUFFING!
THERE'S NO WAY! HE NEVER
GAVE THAT VIBE AT ALL!
WHO? HOW FAR DID
THEY GO? DID HE...</b>

01:22.560 --> 01:23.560
What?

01:25.500 --> 01:26.640
Whoa, there.

01:26.640 --> 01:28.990
Be more careful, would you?

01:28.990 --> 01:29.940
Liar.

01:30.480 --> 01:33.370
Seriously? You're... lying, right?

01:33.690 --> 01:36.200
There's no way a stubborn, 
hyper-efficient, obtuse,

01:36.200 --> 01:38.990
logic-brained loner like you could ever...

01:39.480 --> 01:43.820
Why bother with makeup if you're just 
going to ruin it by opening your mouth?

01:43.820 --> 01:47.780
"Virgin" is a title of respect originating with 
nuns who protected their purity to the end!

01:47.780 --> 01:51.170
And I am not a nun, 
therefore I cannot be a virgin!

01:51.420 --> 01:53.960
Huh? What kind of twisted logic is that?!

01:53.960 --> 01:55.840
It's not twisted logic! It's fact!

01:55.840 --> 01:59.180
So no matter how many times 
I call you a virgin, it won't hurt you?

01:59.180 --> 02:03.120
That means I can call you "Virgin-senpai" 
every day and you won't get mad, right?

02:03.120 --> 02:05.520
Sure, in exchange for me 
punching you in the gut!

02:05.800 --> 02:08.520
See? You're super mad! Hmph!

02:09.720 --> 02:10.940
Hey, Iroha...

02:13.400 --> 02:16.320
Are you really okay with 
revealing your identity?

02:17.770 --> 02:19.070
I am.

02:19.830 --> 02:21.730
Even to Ozu?

02:21.730 --> 02:23.860
Yes. It's okay.

02:24.270 --> 02:27.910
I would've had to tell him 
eventually, anyway. Besides...

02:29.020 --> 02:32.080
I know you'll take care 
of everything in the end.

02:32.400 --> 02:33.770
You know it.

02:33.770 --> 02:37.050
There's a lot I still want you 
to do, after all.

02:37.380 --> 02:39.750
I'm gonna work you to the bone.

02:40.230 --> 02:42.910
Well, there's a proclamation 
of abuse if I ever heard one!

02:42.910 --> 02:46.060
Labor standards inspector! Over here!

02:46.440 --> 02:48.980
Hah! Bring it on if you think you can.

02:51.580 --> 02:55.570
Uh-oh. Did a labor standards 
inspector actually hear me?

02:56.100 --> 02:58.020
Like they'd come here, idiot.

03:03.690 --> 03:04.620
What is it?

03:05.220 --> 03:06.520
Midori-chan...

03:07.190 --> 03:08.660
won't make it in time!

03:08.940 --> 03:09.580
What?!

03:09.580 --> 03:13.580
She left home early because of the weather,

03:13.580 --> 03:19.220
but on her way here, she bumped into a 
woman in labor and had to call an ambulance!

03:19.220 --> 03:24.220
<b>[SUSPENSION OF SERVICE]
SERVICE IS SUSPENDED ON THE INBOUND AND 
OUTBOUND LINES DUE TO LIGHTNING STRIKES.</b>

03:19.480 --> 03:24.610
Then, when she finally got to the station, 
trains were stopped due to the weather!

03:24.610 --> 03:27.100
She couldn't catch a taxi, either!

03:27.640 --> 03:29.610
Could our luck be any worse?

03:29.610 --> 03:31.600
Is this drama club cursed or something?

03:33.170 --> 03:34.270
Ohboshi-kun...

03:34.270 --> 03:37.270
<b>I'M AT THE STATION, BUT THE TRAINS ARE STOPPED AND I
CAN'T EVEN GET A TAXI. WHAT DO I DO? I WON'T MAKE IT!




I'M SORRY, SUMIRE-ONEECHAN.
I'M SORRY, EVERYONE.</b>

03:34.270 --> 03:37.270
<b>CALM DOWN. THANKS FOR TELLING ME.
I'LL LET THE OTHERS KNOW.</b>

03:37.640 --> 03:40.740
President Midori can't make it? Oh, no.

03:41.510 --> 03:43.550
But it's about to start.

03:43.550 --> 03:46.450
We can't start our performance 
without our lead actress.

03:46.450 --> 03:51.410
The drama club... The drama club... 
is gonna turn into the girls' tennis team.

03:52.300 --> 03:54.200
This is looking pretty bad.

03:54.200 --> 03:55.120
Yeah.

03:55.120 --> 03:59.080
I hadn't even considered 
the possibility that she'd be late.

04:01.050 --> 04:02.590
Senpai...

04:03.290 --> 04:06.350
<i>No, there must still be something we can do.</i>

04:06.970 --> 04:07.930
<i>What can we do?</i>

04:08.360 --> 04:10.810
<i>Think. Think...</i>

04:11.850 --> 04:16.020
<i>Who can act decently well 
and knows most of her lines?</i>

04:17.300 --> 04:20.310
Sensei, I'd like to talk to Kageishi-san.

04:20.310 --> 04:22.320
S-Sure, of course.

04:23.540 --> 04:26.820
Midori-chan, Ohboshi-kun wants to talk to you.

04:26.820 --> 04:27.740
I'll put him on.

04:31.310 --> 04:34.950
It's me. So you don't think 
you can get here in time?

04:41.980 --> 04:43.230
Ohboshi-kun...

04:45.480 --> 04:46.540
I'm sorry.

04:47.470 --> 04:49.830
I don't think... I'll make it.

04:51.230 --> 04:52.220
I see.

04:52.580 --> 04:56.190
<i>And after everyone worked 
so hard to get this far.</i>

04:56.850 --> 05:02.020
<i>I... I can't believe I'm ruining 
the day they all worked for.</i>

05:04.350 --> 05:05.200
<i>Everyone...</i>

05:05.820 --> 05:08.180
Ohboshi-kun... I'm sorry.

05:10.040 --> 05:13.200
It's not your fault. It was just bad luck.

05:13.200 --> 05:17.170
No. This always happens with me.

05:17.500 --> 05:20.780
<i>I just act without thinking, 
based on pure emotion.</i>

05:20.780 --> 05:23.080
<i>It makes me screw things up all the time.</i>

05:23.080 --> 05:24.670
<i>I'm well aware of it, you know?</i>

05:25.060 --> 05:28.340
<i>If only I could handle things 
as efficiently as you.</i>

05:29.500 --> 05:31.290
<i>You seem to be operating on a false premise.</i>

05:31.290 --> 05:32.140
Huh?

05:32.140 --> 05:34.260
You haven't done anything wrong.

05:34.260 --> 05:36.600
Not in terms of efficiency or who you are.

05:36.940 --> 05:39.150
But... But I'm...

05:39.450 --> 05:41.800
When I talk about the most efficient method,

05:41.800 --> 05:44.650
I'm talking about the shortest 
route to my own happiness.

05:45.260 --> 05:47.220
If you'd left that pregnant lady alone,

05:47.220 --> 05:50.280
you probably would've regretted it 
for the rest of your life.

05:50.970 --> 05:54.290
The other drama club members have stuck 
with you because that's who you are.

05:54.290 --> 05:55.970
<i>So be proud.</i>

05:55.970 --> 06:01.070
<i>All you did was make the most efficient 
choice for your own way of life.</i>

06:02.330 --> 06:04.550
Ohboshi-kun...

06:05.930 --> 06:09.150
Hey. Do you want to make this play a success?

06:09.510 --> 06:12.470
Of course. That goes without saying.

06:13.670 --> 06:16.230
Even if you can't be here?

06:16.660 --> 06:19.650
Yes! I still want to make it a success!

06:19.960 --> 06:23.610
Sure, it hurts that I can't take 
the stage after working so hard,

06:23.610 --> 06:28.110
<i>but it would hurt three hundred times more 
to ruin everyone else's dreams!</i>

06:29.640 --> 06:31.710
That's what I was hoping to hear.

06:32.340 --> 06:34.590
In that case, there's something we can do.

06:34.590 --> 06:35.240
<i>Huh?</i>

06:38.360 --> 06:40.170
<i>I'll</i> be her stand-in.

06:40.580 --> 06:41.670
What?

06:43.170 --> 06:44.380
It's the lead role!

06:44.680 --> 06:46.980
<i>Do you know all the lines? 
Can you become the character?</i>

06:46.980 --> 06:48.840
It's all stored away in my head.

06:49.150 --> 06:53.850
Of course, my acting skill is pretty 
average, so don't expect too much.

06:54.170 --> 06:56.680
Average? Is that going to be enough?

06:56.990 --> 06:58.660
Oh, I think it will.

06:58.660 --> 07:00.250
"Average" for him is deceptively good.

07:00.250 --> 07:01.100
Huh?

07:01.100 --> 07:02.610
I'm the best at programming,

07:02.610 --> 07:04.890
Murasaki Shikibu-sensei 
is the best at illustration,

07:04.890 --> 07:07.460
and Otoi-san is the best
 when it comes to music,

07:07.460 --> 07:10.720
but Aki can do all of them at 80% of our level.

07:10.720 --> 07:12.110
The same goes for acting, of course.

07:12.610 --> 07:17.290
As advisor, I formally name 
Ohboshi Akiteru as Midori-chan's stand-in!

07:17.290 --> 07:20.210
With Senpai handling it, 
you know we're gonna be just fine.

07:20.210 --> 07:24.170
<i>You have the word of the legendary 
star instructor Iroha-san!</i>

07:24.530 --> 07:26.880
Could you not raise the bar like that, please?

07:27.630 --> 07:30.010
What do you say? Will you let me do it?

07:30.010 --> 07:33.010
<b>ONEE-CHAN</b>

07:32.230 --> 07:33.010
Yes.

07:34.540 --> 07:36.140
Please take good care of them.

07:37.240 --> 07:38.890
What a relief!

07:38.890 --> 07:42.900
I'm glad we turned this into 
a modern story. With our old script...

07:43.220 --> 07:45.100
You can say that again.

07:45.100 --> 07:48.150
The wardrobe never would have worked out.

07:48.150 --> 07:51.300
I am the successor to the world's 
foremost pâtisserie.

07:51.300 --> 07:52.400
That said...

07:53.090 --> 07:56.280
a little makeup sure makes 
a big difference on you, huh?

07:57.850 --> 07:59.700
You look pretty good.

08:00.130 --> 08:01.120
You think so?

08:01.120 --> 08:06.060
Yep! Maybe this will inspire you 
to wear makeup every day!

08:06.060 --> 08:07.600
I'm gonna pass on that.

08:07.600 --> 08:09.480
I'd waste too much time every morning.

08:09.480 --> 08:11.610
Hey! Don't call it wasting time!

08:11.610 --> 08:14.090
Girls put makeup on every morning, you know!

08:14.630 --> 08:19.490
Though you do have nice skin, 
so you don't really need it, but still...

08:19.490 --> 08:20.180
Yes?

08:21.050 --> 08:22.980
Next group, please prepare to go on stage.

08:31.880 --> 08:32.780
Okay.

08:32.780 --> 08:35.530
Remember, everyone! Remain calm!

08:35.530 --> 08:37.930
As long as you keep your cool, 
victory is within reach!

08:37.930 --> 08:40.790
The drama club will <i>not</i> turn 
into the girls' tennis team!

08:41.080 --> 08:43.850
Couldn't you come up with a better pep talk?

08:46.440 --> 08:48.570
Ready, everyone?

08:49.450 --> 08:51.290
Aim for victory!

08:51.290 --> 08:52.970
Yeah!

09:00.460 --> 09:03.980
Hey, you don't need to be so tense, Senpai.

09:04.890 --> 09:09.940
If you make any mistakes, 
I'll back you up, my cute hero!

09:09.940 --> 09:14.710
You got that backwards. 
Let me back <i>you</i> up, you uncute heroine.

09:20.990 --> 09:24.000
<b>MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER HAS IT IN FOR ME!</b>

09:26.800 --> 09:29.840
<i>A script I wrote is about 
to be performed as a play.</i>

09:30.530 --> 09:35.270
<i>I wrote it as an event scenario 
for 05th Floor Alliance</i>

09:36.110 --> 09:39.470
<i>with the intent of conveying 
my honest feelings to Aki.</i>

09:39.960 --> 09:43.140
<i>I think it's the best one 
I've come up with yet.</i>

09:44.130 --> 09:48.600
<i>And Iroha-chan ended up standing in 
for the heroine's role on short notice, right?</i>

10:06.540 --> 10:09.500
<i>W-Wow... This is high quality!</i>

10:12.820 --> 10:14.420
<i>It's Iroha-chan...</i>

10:14.420 --> 10:18.590
This is the story of my first love.

10:18.930 --> 10:23.320
I never believed in fate at all

10:23.820 --> 10:26.280
until I had that fateful encounter.

10:33.730 --> 10:36.150
Fate? Don't be silly.

10:36.610 --> 10:39.150
Life is something you shape 
with your own hands!

10:39.150 --> 10:41.530
I always thought that fate and destiny

10:41.530 --> 10:44.660
were just excuses invoked by those who 
couldn't make their dreams come true.

10:45.220 --> 10:46.820
<i>Why is Aki...</i>

10:47.160 --> 10:49.670
You don't take baking seriously, do you?

10:49.950 --> 10:53.630
That isn't my intent. 
I'm simply thinking in terms of efficiency.

10:53.970 --> 10:56.130
<i>Their parents hate each other.</i>

10:56.860 --> 11:00.840
<i>Their first meeting 
was characterized by animosity.</i>

11:01.190 --> 11:02.180
Hmph!

11:09.950 --> 11:11.440
Hey! What are you doing?

11:11.440 --> 11:14.480
I'm sorry! I had something on my mind.

11:15.270 --> 11:18.440
Is there something bothering you?

11:19.690 --> 11:21.850
If you don't mind talking to me, 
I am glad to listen.

11:22.930 --> 11:24.370
The truth is, I...

11:25.380 --> 11:28.870
I've... been hiding something from you.

11:28.870 --> 11:34.880
<i>Yes. This is where she confronts him 
with the feelings she's kept secret.</i>

11:35.700 --> 11:40.570
<i>Then, as the two of them 
work their hardest to make the cake,</i>

11:40.570 --> 11:42.340
<i>they're drawn to each other.</i>

11:42.680 --> 11:44.670
You're amazing.

11:44.670 --> 11:45.470
Huh?

11:46.180 --> 11:49.120
I never knew you could make 
such delicate decorations.

11:49.770 --> 11:54.400
I... just didn't want 
to hold you back, so I...

11:54.900 --> 11:56.900
I think you have an incredible talent.

11:57.930 --> 11:58.820
Really?

11:59.730 --> 12:01.890
Let's win that competition together.

12:01.890 --> 12:03.000
Right!

12:03.000 --> 12:08.720
<i>Aki and Iroha-chan are breathing life 
into the lines I wrote.</i>

12:12.700 --> 12:14.670
Here, eat up!

12:15.650 --> 12:16.750
It's so sweet!

12:17.300 --> 12:21.170
The moment it hit my tongue, 
an elegant sweetness filled my mouth.

12:21.530 --> 12:23.420
And now you.

12:24.570 --> 12:27.160
This faint aroma I smell...

12:27.160 --> 12:29.160
That's vanilla bean, isn't it?

12:29.160 --> 12:31.640
The mellow flavor satisfies my very soul!

12:31.960 --> 12:34.100
I can't believe how delicate it is!

12:34.100 --> 12:36.020
It's... just like you!

12:36.020 --> 12:38.650
This sensation, like I'm being embraced...

12:39.210 --> 12:40.940
It feels like you!

12:40.940 --> 12:42.060
Don't move.

12:42.060 --> 12:43.820
<i>Aki and Iroha-chan...</i>

12:43.820 --> 12:44.560
Huh?

12:44.560 --> 12:45.820
<i>...are breathing life...</i>

12:45.820 --> 12:46.620
Wha—

12:46.620 --> 12:48.810
<i>...into the lines I wrote.</i>

12:49.650 --> 12:53.080
<i>Wait, what kind of sparkly,
 saccharine script is this? It's ridiculous.</i>

12:53.450 --> 12:56.120
<i>This is way too much brain-melting romance.</i>

12:56.120 --> 12:59.090
<i>It's so stupid. Who came up with...</i>

13:00.050 --> 13:01.840
<i>N-No way!</i>

13:01.840 --> 13:04.090
<i>I made Aki read this?!</i>

13:04.090 --> 13:05.590
<i>Oh, no! This is hell!</i>

13:08.510 --> 13:10.430
<i>I'm so embarrassed that I could die!</i>

13:11.330 --> 13:13.950
I can't attend this school any longer.

13:13.950 --> 13:17.220
I won't be able to stay with you anymore.

13:17.880 --> 13:18.940
But...

13:21.620 --> 13:22.690
Goodbye.

13:25.330 --> 13:26.030
No!

13:26.580 --> 13:29.110
Are you just going to let 
your talents go to waste?!

13:29.110 --> 13:29.830
Huh?

13:30.340 --> 13:34.250
Then I'll create a place where 
you can make your talents shine!

13:34.250 --> 13:34.830
So please...

13:35.300 --> 13:39.900
<i>This conversation sounds like 
the real Aki and Iroha-chan talking.</i>

13:40.420 --> 13:42.210
<i>How do they do it?</i>

13:42.210 --> 13:46.320
<i>It's like they're partners who've 
been practicing together for years.</i>

13:46.970 --> 13:48.430
I love you.

13:50.250 --> 13:52.470
<i>Iroha-chan's face just now...</i>

13:53.030 --> 13:55.450
<i>As a girl myself, I can tell.</i>

13:55.450 --> 13:59.560
<i>I think I recognize it because 
we both fell for the same guy.</i>

13:59.970 --> 14:05.700
<i>Up until now, I believed what they said 
and thought maybe it wasn't true.</i>

14:05.700 --> 14:07.170
<i>But I was wrong.</i>

14:07.170 --> 14:08.990
<i>This is definitely...</i>

14:09.500 --> 14:12.410
I'm in love with you.

14:13.070 --> 14:14.970
<i>Tell me, Iroha-chan...</i>

14:14.970 --> 14:18.700
<i>Is that the line I wrote for the heroine?</i>

14:18.700 --> 14:20.170
<i>Or is it...</i>

14:20.940 --> 14:22.090
I...

14:23.160 --> 14:25.090
love you, too.

14:25.800 --> 14:30.090
<i>I don't know how Aki feels 
about Iroha-chan, but...</i>

14:30.650 --> 14:35.100
<i>Iroha-chan... when you make that face...</i>

14:36.010 --> 14:37.610
<i>It's too obvious.</i>

14:55.860 --> 14:59.640
But I can't be with you! It's not allowed!

14:59.640 --> 15:01.120
That's my fate!

15:01.770 --> 15:04.090
There's no fate where I can't be with you!

15:04.090 --> 15:07.090
We have to stay together forever!

15:07.410 --> 15:08.560
Then...

15:09.110 --> 15:12.010
Then get out of my sight!

15:12.280 --> 15:15.470
No... If you can't do that...

15:15.840 --> 15:17.390
then <i>I'll</i> disappear!

15:18.040 --> 15:24.680
I can tell what's behind your words 
and actions right now.

15:26.450 --> 15:30.400
I'm not just looking at who you 
are on the outside anymore.

15:30.790 --> 15:34.220
I know the true feelings lying behind it.

15:34.700 --> 15:35.410
So...

15:37.830 --> 15:41.520
It's true! Even if my parents disown me...

15:41.520 --> 15:44.280
Even if the whole world turns against me...

15:45.430 --> 15:50.440
Even if the world ends, I... I...

15:45.510 --> 15:47.340
<i>I'm not acting right now.</i>

15:47.340 --> 15:50.840
<i>This is my chance 
to tell Senpai how I truly feel!</i>

15:51.910 --> 15:53.150
Senpai!

15:53.590 --> 15:56.310
I love you!

15:59.210 --> 16:02.890
<i>Iroha-chan chan looks truly happy 
from the bottom of her heart</i>

16:02.890 --> 16:06.040
<i>after confronting Aki with her feelings.</i>

16:06.490 --> 16:09.900
<i>Seeing her like that even makes me happy.</i>

16:28.210 --> 16:31.580
<i>But at the same time, 
when I realize it's Aki she's saying it to,</i>

16:31.580 --> 16:33.930
<i>something inside me feels all wrong.</i>

16:34.790 --> 16:39.390
<i>Which feeling am I supposed 
to be honest about?</i>

16:45.100 --> 16:48.940
I never would've guessed Iroha 
had such a talent for acting.

16:49.260 --> 16:51.150
Yeah, I guess.

16:51.150 --> 16:54.400
You knew about her, didn't you?

16:54.890 --> 16:56.130
Yeah.

16:56.130 --> 16:58.960
I can't believe you guys 
kept it secret all this time.

17:00.530 --> 17:04.050
Iroha's feelings were pretty obvious 
in her acting, though, huh?

17:04.050 --> 17:06.260
And they're not dating? Hard to believe.

17:06.260 --> 17:08.210
Well, Aki's pretty dense.

17:08.210 --> 17:14.800
<b>ROOM YOU CAN'T LEAVE UNLESS YOU KISS</b>

17:08.600 --> 17:14.230
How about we help them out by putting them 
in a room they can't leave unless they kiss?

17:15.160 --> 17:17.760
All right! I'll come up 
with a suitable scheme!

17:18.300 --> 17:22.180
You can be pretty scary 
sometimes, you know that?

17:33.070 --> 17:35.990
That was fantastic!

17:35.990 --> 17:37.910
Thank you so much!

17:38.870 --> 17:41.610
I have to apologize to you, 
Ohboshi-kun and Kohinata-san.

17:41.610 --> 17:44.620
You had to be in the play 
because of my own failings.

17:44.620 --> 17:47.290
I didn't mind at all!

17:47.290 --> 17:50.480
It was fun getting to act on such a big stage!

17:50.480 --> 17:52.060
Yeah, true.

17:52.060 --> 17:55.090
It was a valuable experience 
for us, so don't sweat it.

17:55.090 --> 17:56.960
Everyone, let's work hard on the next one, too!

17:56.960 --> 17:58.050
Yeah!

17:58.050 --> 18:03.230
Oh, right. I'd like to thank Makigai 
Namako-sensei for the script, too.

18:03.230 --> 18:05.940
Sure. I'd be happy to pass that on.

18:05.940 --> 18:07.140
Thanks.

18:10.730 --> 18:16.360
<b>HOW WAS THE COMPETITION? I KNOW MY SCRIPT WASN'T GREAT... THERE'S SO MUCH I WISH I'D DONE DIFFERENTLY. 

I'M REALLY SORRY. I DIDN'T REALIZE I'D SENT YOU SOMETHING THAT EMBARRASSING.</b>

18:16.360 --> 18:17.610
<b>I'M REALLY SORRY. I DIDN'T REALIZE I'D SENT YOU SOMETHING THAT EMBARRASSING.
(READ)</b>

18:23.130 --> 18:25.330
Ohboshi-kun!

18:25.330 --> 18:29.790
Now I won't have to coach the 
girls' tennis team! I'm sure of it!

18:29.790 --> 18:31.570
Thank you!

18:31.570 --> 18:34.910
Thank you so much for everything!

18:40.300 --> 18:43.860
Are you sure we don't need to be at 
 the award ceremony?

18:43.860 --> 18:45.180
I'm sure.

18:45.180 --> 18:47.660
We were just helpers.

18:47.660 --> 18:49.690
The trophy belongs to them.

18:49.690 --> 18:53.170
That could've been a priceless chance 
to stand up there looking smug.

18:53.170 --> 18:55.780
I only helped the drama club in the first place

18:55.780 --> 18:59.450
to solve all of 05th Floor Alliance's 
problems at once.

18:59.450 --> 19:02.930
Now Murasaki Shikibu-sensei 
can focus on her illustrations,

19:02.930 --> 19:07.900
and the screenplay from Makigai Namako-sensei 
that I had to reject got some use.

19:07.900 --> 19:12.290
I don't know why Makigai-sensei 
had so many regrets about it,

19:12.290 --> 19:13.750
but it all worked out in the end.

19:13.750 --> 19:17.800
That's my Senpai! 
It was the most efficient method, right?

19:17.800 --> 19:20.700
The drama club has the prefectural 
competition to work toward next,

19:20.700 --> 19:23.260
and we have <i>Black Goat</i>'s reputation to work on.

19:23.260 --> 19:26.800
We're putting our talents to the test 
in two very different venues.

19:26.800 --> 19:28.980
Save the smug faces until then.

19:29.290 --> 19:30.840
Fine.

19:31.770 --> 19:35.730
By the way, Senpai, aren't you 
forgetting something important?

19:35.730 --> 19:36.690
Huh?

19:36.690 --> 19:38.830
Come on, you know there's something!

19:38.830 --> 19:40.960
This was your star pupil's big day!

19:40.960 --> 19:43.960
I did my job brilliantly 
in front of all those people!

19:43.960 --> 19:45.480
Glance, glance...

19:45.480 --> 19:48.450
Good job. You worked hard.

19:50.300 --> 19:52.370
Thank you!

19:52.370 --> 19:54.920
That's not nearly enough, though!

19:54.920 --> 19:56.830
Put more spirit into your praise!

19:56.830 --> 19:58.760
Don't push your luck.

19:59.190 --> 20:01.670
Hey, wait up!

20:01.670 --> 20:05.070
Anyway, your idea of "average" 
really is deceptively good, huh?

20:05.070 --> 20:07.080
Your acting was solid, 
plain and simple.

20:07.080 --> 20:10.800
I studied the basics of 
acting in middle school.

20:10.800 --> 20:13.230
I always helped you practice, too.

20:13.230 --> 20:15.740
And that was enough to make you this good.

20:15.740 --> 20:18.780
I think you could claim a little 
more limelight, personally.

20:19.140 --> 20:21.550
Do you have time to talk about me?

20:21.550 --> 20:24.740
What about you? How did you 
like being in the spotlight?

20:24.740 --> 20:28.660
Honestly... I was a little scared.

20:29.490 --> 20:31.960
What would I have done if Mom found out?

20:31.960 --> 20:35.120
I was sure she'd turn out to be 
somewhere in the audience.

20:36.330 --> 20:39.940
But because you took my hand and guided me,

20:39.940 --> 20:42.220
I was able to just enjoy acting.

20:42.680 --> 20:43.700
Iroha...

20:43.700 --> 20:46.510
U-Um, you know, Senpai...

20:47.380 --> 20:50.600
I'm the sort of actor who 
completely embodies the character.

20:50.600 --> 20:54.170
The heroine's lines... weren't just lines.

20:54.740 --> 20:57.310
They were... my real...

20:57.610 --> 21:00.440
Um... Iroha?

21:00.780 --> 21:02.150
Are you saying...

21:05.060 --> 21:06.700
Gotcha!

21:06.700 --> 21:10.010
Did you get excited? Was your heart pounding?

21:10.010 --> 21:10.660
Wha...

21:12.070 --> 21:15.330
I guess I earned favorability 
points with you yet again!

21:15.330 --> 21:17.670
Mwah! Sorry I'm so cute!

21:17.670 --> 21:20.090
You were messing with me <i>again?!</i>

21:21.150 --> 21:24.920
You haven't even seen the <i>beginning</i> 
of me messing with you!

21:26.810 --> 21:30.570
I'm gonna keep showing you 
more and more of the real me!

21:30.570 --> 21:32.930
So stick with me, okay, Senpai?

21:35.880 --> 21:39.580
I swear, she's such a pain.

21:40.530 --> 21:49.410
<i>Seriously, why are all the people 
who associate with me so infuriating?</i>

21:52.290 --> 21:54.290
<b>Translation: Becky Cottrill</b>

21:54.290 --> 21:57.080
<b>Subtitle Editing: Geoff Mazzolini
Subtitle Timing: Krzysztof Kunc</b>

21:57.290 --> 21:59.960
<b>Quality Control: Gabriella Ramirez
Translation Check: David Saylor</b>

22:15.600 --> 22:21.340
<b>MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER HAS IT IN FOR ME!</b>

23:21.500 --> 23:25.960
<b>THANK YOU FOR WATCHING</b>
